    "e1737905-910b-4240-a9c5-18766d656dbf": {
      "type": "page__text-with-table",
      "blocks": {
        "template--15036906930255__e1737905-910b-4240-a9c5-18766d656dbf-text-1": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "",
            "title2": "How is the Diamond Hybrid created?",
            "heading_size": "regular",
            "text": "<p>The Diamond Hybrid is created by placing a perfectly-cut crystal core or substrate into a chamber of intense heat and pressure and infusing lab-created diamond crystals, or bonding them at a molecular level, into the outer layers of the crystal core. These lab created diamond crystals stack up on the core and realign with each other. The finished product is a diamond-infused simulant with a nonprecious crystal core and a solid outer layer of lab-created diamond that will never wear off or detach from the core.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "link": "",
            "button_style": "button--primary",
            "background": "rgba(0,0,0,0)",
            "text_color": "rgba(0,0,0,0)",
            "alignment": "left",
            "vertical_position": "center"
          }
        },
